---
title: "Import a project onto another device"
sidebar:
  order: 7
---

Create a local project from a NAHPU transfer or recover a project on a replacement device.

## Steps

{% steps %}

1. Keep the source archive and back up any existing data on the receiving installation.
2. On the home screen, select `Import project`, then `Choose archive`. Select a project JSON.GZ, ZIP, TAR.GZ, or compatible NAHPU Data Package.
3. Review the project identity and `Destination project name`. If the project UUID already exists, use `Open Merge project`; a different project with the same name needs a distinct destination name.
4. Acknowledge the backup reminder, review personnel, taxonomy, and specimens, and resolve every item marked `Needs attention`.
5. Review counts and missing-file warnings, then select `Import project` at the final review.
6. Open the imported project and check sites, events, specimen identifiers, narratives, and several attachments. JSON.GZ does not contain media; retain the source until verification is complete.
{% /steps %}

